tasks.description:
Replace the stub `GetSchemaAndBuildAssembly` in `DatabricksDriver.cs` with a real implementation.

**Part 1 — Schema Explorer tree:**
Read `WorkspaceUrl`, decrypt PAT, read `WarehouseId`, `DefaultCatalog`, `DefaultSchema` from `cxInfo.DriverData`. Construct `DatabricksHttpClient` + `UnityCatalogClient`. Call them synchronously (`.GetAwaiter().GetResult()`) since this method is not async.

Build the `List<ExplorerItem>` tree:
- One item per catalog: `ExplorerItemKind.Schema`, `ExplorerIcon.Schema`, `Text = catalog.Name`, children populated below.
- Under each catalog: one item per schema: `ExplorerItemKind.Schema`, `ExplorerIcon.Schema`, children populated below.
- Under each schema: tables as `ExplorerItemKind.QueryableObject`, `ExplorerIcon.Blank`; views (`TableType` == `VIEW` or `MATERIALIZED_VIEW`) as `ExplorerItemKind.QueryableObject`, `ExplorerIcon.TableFunction`.
- If `DefaultCatalog`/`DefaultSchema` are set, sort them to the top of their respective lists.

**Part 2 — Typed context assembly:**
Generate minimal C# source:
```csharp
namespace {nameSpace} {{
    public class {typeName} {{
        private readonly LinqPad.Databricks.Driver.Sql.StatementExecutionClient _exec;
        public {typeName}(LinqPad.Databricks.Driver.Sql.StatementExecutionClient exec) {{ _exec = exec; }}
        // One dynamic IEnumerable property per table/view (optional for initial pass)
    }}
}}
```
For the initial pass, an empty context class is acceptable — the important output is the `ExplorerItem` tree. Use `CompileSource(new CompilationInput { SourceCode = new[] { src }, FilePathsToReference = GetCoreFxReferenceAssemblies().Append(typeof(DatabricksDriver).Assembly.Location).ToArray(), OutputPath = assemblyToBuild.CodeBase })`. Set `nameSpace = "LinqPad.Databricks"` and `typeName = "DatabricksContext"`.

**Error handling:** If UC API calls fail (network, auth), catch and return an empty list with a single `ExplorerItem` showing the error text — never let exceptions escape `GetSchemaAndBuildAssembly` unhandled.

**Acceptance:** `dotnet build` succeeds. In LINQPad (manual test), Schema Explorer shows catalog/schema/table hierarchy. `GetLastSchemaUpdate` override is optional but add a stub returning `null`.
